abstract: "A deterministic, lifecycle-based compliance-as-code framework for validating one-time-passcode (OTP) multi-factor authentication over email and SMS channels against PCI-DSS v4.0.1 and NIST SP 800-63B-4 controls. OTP is modeled as an explicit state machine (generated, valid, then expired, consumed, superseded, or locked), with each regulatory requirement mapped to a specific, testable state transition and evaluated via a deterministic PASS/FAIL/INCONCLUSIVE policy engine. The framework supports two interchangeable OTP delivery-capture adapters, a real external email/SMS capture service and a local in-memory simulator, so the same lifecycle assertions and compliance mapping validate identically against either. A companion statistical/ML research layer evaluates control-violation prediction, feature and control ablation, delayed-OTP TTL boundary behavior under jitter, and OTP comparison timing side-channels, on synthetic, seeded, and explicitly disclosed data. Proven via 9 passing Playwright-BDD end-to-end scenarios covering 6 cited controls."
